---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { TOOLS } from '../data/tools';
---
<Base
  title="About"
  description="What Edexcel IAL Arsenal is, who it is for, and how it works."
  status={{ label: 'About', hint: 'What this site is and how it works.' }}
  stats={[{ label: 'Tools', value: TOOLS.length }]}
>
  <article class="panel prose rise">
    <div class="about-head">
      <img src="/brand/ial-arsenal-logo-colorful.svg" width="84" height="84" alt="Edexcel IAL Arsenal logo" />
      <div><p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h2>Study tools for Edexcel IAL sciences</h2></div>
    </div>
    <p>Edexcel IAL Arsenal is a growing set of free tools for students taking Pearson Edexcel International A Levels in Chemistry and Physics. Each one covers part of the specification you would otherwise have to memorise from a page: you run the reactions, test yourself and see what changes.</p>

    <h3>What you'll find</h3>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Simulations</b>: virtual benches and labs where you try things and see the result.</li>
      <li><b>Drills</b>: short self-tests with a running score.</li>
      <li><b>References</b>: the facts you need, laid out so they're quick to check.</li>
    </ul>

    <h3>How it works</h3>
    <p>Everything runs in your browser. There are no accounts. Your theme, scores and progress are saved on this device only.</p>
    <p>Pick a palette from the theme button at the top. Your choice follows you into every tool.</p>

    <h3>Accuracy</h3>
    <p>Content follows the current Edexcel IAL specifications and spellings (sulfur, aluminium, colourless).</p>

    <h3>Who makes it</h3>
    <p>Edexcel IAL Arsenal is made by <a href="https://github.com/TheCodeHeist">Md Riyasat Hossain</a> (TheCodeHeist on GitHub), an Edexcel IAL student who took Chemistry and Physics. It started as the kind of practice he wanted while revising, and it's built for the students taking these papers now.</p>

    <h3>Biology, and helping out</h3>
    <p>There are no Biology tools yet, because nobody maintaining the site has taken Biology. If you have and would like to co-maintain it, you're welcome: the project is open source on <a href="https://github.com/TheCodeHeist/edexcel-ial-arsenal">GitHub</a>. Fixes and new tools for Chemistry and Physics are welcome too.</p>

    <h3>Not affiliated</h3>
    <p>This is an independent project. It is not produced, endorsed or checked by Pearson Edexcel. Use it alongside the official specification, past papers and mark schemes, not instead of them.</p>
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .about-head { display: flex; gap: 18px; align-items: center; margin-bottom: 8px; }
  .about-head img { flex: none; border-radius: 10px; }
  .about-head h2 { margin: 0; }
</style>
